#ROOM
Vnum     40401
Name     Qigong Kesh Landing Pad~
Sector   desert~
Flags    can_land~
Desc     A wide, wind-scoured pad marks the only real landing site
anywhere near Qigong Kesh, its surface pitted from decades of engine
wash and blowing sand. No permanent structure stands here - just the
pad itself, and the long walk into the Silent Desert beyond.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40402
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    40936
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40402
Name     The Silent Desert~
Sector   desert~
Flags    ~
Desc     Pale dunes stretch in every direction, utterly still beneath a
sky too bright to look at directly. Even the wind seems muted here,
as though the desert itself is holding its breath. Qigong Kesh's
walls are just visible ahead, shimmering faintly in the heat.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    40401
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40403
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40403
Name     Gate of Qigong Kesh~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Qigong Kesh's gate is low and unadorned, built more for shelter
from the desert than for grandeur. A faint hum of concentrated
stillness seems to radiate from the Temple beyond, even from here.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    40402
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40404
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40404
Name     Central Meditation Hall~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A wide, circular hall forms the heart of Qigong Kesh, its floor
covered in woven sand-cushions arranged in careful concentric rings.
Initiates sit scattered throughout, most with eyes closed, reaching
for senses beyond the ordinary five.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    40403
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40405
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    40406
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    40408
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40403 2 40404
Reset O 0 40401 5 40404
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40405
Name     Meditation Chamber - Alpha~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A small, private chamber, kept deliberately bare of anything
that might draw the eye or the mind. Initiates come here alone, when
the Central Hall's shared stillness isn't quiet enough.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    40404
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40406
Name     Meditation Chamber - Beta~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Identical in every visible respect to its twin chamber elsewhere
in the Temple, this room's only distinction is its use - reserved for
initiates working under an instructor's direct supervision.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    40404
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    40407
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40402 1 40406
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40407
Name     Miarta Sek's Sanctum~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The stillest room in a Temple built entirely around stillness,
Miarta Sek's sanctum holds nothing but a single cushion and bare
walls. She receives visitors here rarely, and never for long.
~
#EXIT
Direction down~
ToRoom    40406
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40401 1 40407
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40408
Name     Sensory Deprivation Chamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Utterly dark and near-silent, this chamber strips away sight and
sound alike, leaving only the Force to navigate by. Few initiates last
their first hour here without reaching for a wall that isn't there.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    40404
#ENDEXIT

Reset O 0 40402 3 40408
#ENDROOM

